ontainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514409#post1514409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Confirmed up thread, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Four extra Health Boxes for when you're in Crinos.</div> </div> </div> </div>...derp, thank you.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I have to say, how effin' in a hurry you have to be to trace a goddamn alien from a movie to stand in for a human-formed werewolf??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 06-10-2023, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T00:04:06-07:00","id":1514412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514409#post1514409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Confirmed up thread, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose i should be grateful theyre using a celebrity but goddamn that's lazy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T00:24:17-07:00","id":1514415,"title":"","content":"There was already a picture that's fairly obviously a trace of Idris Elba's Heimdall from the MCU as well, so this wouldn't be the first humanoid MCU alien traced for a werewolf in the book we've seen.<br /> <br /> Also, from what we can gather so far... the art was in a hell of a hurry with lots of art for multiple WOD5e books at once, and Paradox's odd insistence on GenCon releases.<br /> <br /> I'm really unsure of what's going to happen if Disney decides to squish Paradox over this. Esp. since I'm sure Disney would love to take a pot shot at DC for their recent WtA IP infringement (they used the terms glabro and crinos to describe a werewolf-Jimmy Olsen's forms) that Paradox probably can't afford to do. I dread the idea of the WoD somehow ending up in the hands of The House of Mouse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T00:37:13-07:00","id":1514416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514415#post1514415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I dread the idea of the WoD somehow ending up in the hands of The House of Mouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being 'like Forsaken/CoD' would be least of your problems when House of Mouse come for yeah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To me, as CoD fan, it's really interesting - but also weird - they steal A LOT from Forsaken. Like, they do get those games to explore those street level ideas we in CoD like...<br /> <br /> Well, no. Paradox, unofficially of course, killed CoD gameline. No press release, no media spotlight - but it's 5th year without new books announcements for CoD. And Onyx Path seems to only end their writing for books already in pipeline till 2018.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T00:41:24-07:00","id":1514417,"title":"","content":"Reading up on the whole topic of using photo-references and tracing, one thing that immediately stuck out to me was that you could easily tell someone was just tracing photos when they're quickly producing multiple drawings in a short period of time. And so when this one guy is delivering this huge pile of work for not just the W5 corebook but also the V5 Players Guide <i>and </i>the first H5 supplement (plus, I assume, stuff for the upcoming Blood Sigils), shouldn't there have been alarm bells be going off in the Art Director's head...? There's no way this guy could produce this much art in such a short period of time if he's only using the photos as a reference...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T01:13:40-07:00","id":1514421,"title":"","content":"Why don't we still have a character piece that's a Crinos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T01:50:36-07:00","id":1514427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514421#post1514421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't we still have a character piece that's a Crinos?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe because no one will ever voluntarily transform to Crinos with the mechanics in place?<br /> <br /> Also there's less traceable Crinos art out there....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T02:01:39-07:00","id":1514430,"title":"","content":"I wanted to ask if there might be a higher res sheet to read, but I didn't dare edit the post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T02:07:44-07:00","id":1514432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514430#post1514430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to ask if there might be a higher res sheet to read, but I didn't dare edit the post.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, no. I grabbed the images from the stream and so far none of these previews have been posted elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T02:30:10-07:00","id":1514436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514415#post1514415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, from what we can gather so far... the art was in a hell of a hurry with lots of art for multiple WOD5e books at once, and Paradox's odd insistence on GenCon releases.</div> </div> </div> </div>It all makes me ponder how bad is the art direction if a single artist is tasked to do multiple big profile books in such quick succession.<br /> <br /> I mean, tracing from pics you did not buy to use is still bad and the tone deafness of some traces hurts the book. But if the artist truly was in a hurry, it can explain somewhat why things are like this.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T03:39:11-07:00","id":1514441,"title":"","content":"I only recently discovered a love for Hare's Leap - for some reason it's been nerfed beyond all recognition here, unless the shorthand version on the sheet is misleading.<br /> <br /> Drax was my very first thought when I saw the Ahroun image. The writeup is also just... bad.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fuck you, Wyrm. </div> </div> </div>It's so juvenile, it's so instantly memeable, it's so... well it's just cringey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ahroun wreck shit and tear out throats. </div> </div> </div>This feels like a 90's American type thing - I can imagine a stereotypical Trailer Voiceover reading this line. It's BADASS! EPIC BACON CHUCK NORRIS!<br /> <br /> My boy is a Child of Gaia, Metis, Ahroun, so I'm sure you can imagine that W5 hasn't won a friend in me thus far. I can't wait to see the Children of Gaia preview!<br /> <br /> Most obvious ways it can go wrong are &quot;Apocalypse is so close the Tribe have given up on peace&quot; and stereotypical tree-hugging hippy, so I'm guessing it'll be one of those.<br /> <br /> Anyways, here's a quote from a W20 book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those who enter this world under Luna\u2019s full light are a force to be reckoned with. There is no half-measure with an Ahroun, no hesitation, no uncertainty. They are in all things wholly what they are, be it warrior or leader, protector or executioner. The fire inside us all burns brightest in the full-moon soul, a flame that both fuels them and threatens to consume them, should they not be strong enough to survive the heat.<br /> <br /> In every challenge, be it for sport or survival, Ahroun are found in the forefront, showing others the way forward. They willingly take on the harshest tasks, those that would break the bodies or spirits of weaker beings. In every great battle, every raid, every ambush, the full-moons bear the harshest weight for the sake of their brethren. They are the fiercest foe, and the most passionate protectors, and without them, our sacred duty would have no hope of being fulfilled.<br /> <br /> Theirs is the way of fire, and like fire, they are capable of all extremes. They can illuminate and protect. They can inspire fear.<br /> <br /> Or they can destroy. </div> </div> </div>You can barely tell the difference!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 06-10-2023, 07:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T03:58:23-07:00","id":1514445,"title":"","content":"BTW does anyone have a link to this preview being posted on twitter? Or a link to people finding the trace origins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T04:42:39-07:00","id":1514449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514441#post1514441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a 90's American type thing - I can imagine a stereotypical Trailer Voiceover reading this line. It's BADASS! EPIC BACON CHUCK NORRIS!</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the style reminded me of the Birthday Boys sketch about <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4nL5AMQAVsU\" target=\"_blank\">this bizarro-version of Star Wars</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514441#post1514441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My boy is a Child of Gaia, Metis, Ahroun, so I'm sure you can imagine that W5 hasn't won a friend in me thus far. I can't wait to see the Children of Gaia preview!<br /> <br /> Most obvious ways it can go wrong are &quot;Apocalypse is so close the Tribe have given up on peace&quot; and stereotypical tree-hugging hippy, so I'm guessing it'll be one of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>The text from the Tribe-cards goes like this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Children Of Gaia concern themselves with the greater mysteries of their namesake, seeking to understand the enigmas that exist in her presence. A Child of Gaia is challenged by nothing so much as a mystery to investigate or a wound, literal or figurative, to mend and they are especially drawn to the esoteric Umbra. </div> </div> </div>Like usual, hard to tell how that's different from the Ghost Council interest in secrets/mysteries or the Silent Strider's interest in the Umbra...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> BTW does anyone have a link to this preview being posted on twitter? Or a link to people finding the trace origins? </div> </div> </div>I don't know if <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar479_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"479\" data-vbnamecard=\"479\">Damian May</a> has found something better but I mean everybody knows it's Drax. I have found no photo of Dave Bautista as Drax that looks exactly like the image we got in the preview here. But I think I've found something else that has served as the photo-reference here: it's the head of a Drax-action-figure.<br /> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><img width=\"630\" height=\"698\" data-align=\"center\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/82VuEJL.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/82VuEJL.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/82VuEJL.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div><br /> <br /> Not 100% sure but what do people think? Was this the photo-reference?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T05:37:12-07:00","id":1514451,"title":"","content":"<img width=\"1629\" height=\"1035\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/qPnZCCJ.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qPnZCCJ.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/qPnZCCJ.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> I got a bigger capture so it's easier to discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T05:52:20-07:00","id":1514454,"title":"","content":"So let me get some things straight.<br /> You can have max 5 Rage.<br /> Getting in touch with your Touchstone lowers it to 1.<br /> You need to make Rage checks to transform into anything more than a Wolf or a Human. Two checks if you want the iconic Crinos form.<br /> To Regenerate health in these forms, you need to do a Rage check.<br /> On top of all of this, in Crinos you need to spend Willpower every turn or you will Frenzy like no tomorrow.<br /> Oh and Crinos form automatically fails Stealth and Social.<br /> <br /> All I am going to say is that if writers want to write Human: The Outcast or something, they should stop mudding waters by pretending to be Werewolf the Apocalypse.<br /> It is so bad that Example character only has 3 Willpower (meaning only 3 Turns of non-Frenzy Crinos) and no Rage (I assume that's what the empty Rage boxes imply) thus can't even transform outside of Lupus and Homid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T05:57:14-07:00","id":1514455,"title":"","content":"It probably works like Hunger. So when you shift to Crinos you get two rage checks. You don't spend points, you get more points of rage making you less controllable and nastier to people around you until you hang out with someone to vent it. Also just now did I realise this kinda sounds like you take it out on the touchstones, but they probably meant it more about them being soothing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T06:22:14-07:00","id":1514457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514455#post1514455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably works like Hunger. So when you shift to Crinos you get two rage checks. You don't spend points, you get more points of rage making you less controllable and nastier to people around you until you hang out with someone to vent it. Also just now did I realise this kinda sounds like you take it out on the touchstones, but they probably meant it more about them being soothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds...unworkable, to the point that Crinos form looks more like a punishment. Especially with how you will spend Willpower like water.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T06:23:13-07:00","id":1514458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514417#post1514417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading up on the whole topic of using photo-references and tracing, one thing that immediately stuck out to me was that you could easily tell someone was just tracing photos when they're quickly producing multiple drawings in a short period of time. And so when this one guy is delivering this huge pile of work for not just the W5 corebook but also the V5 Players Guide <i>and </i>the first H5 supplement (plus, I assume, stuff for the upcoming Blood Sigils), shouldn't there have been alarm bells be going off in the Art Director's head...? There's no way this guy could produce this much art in such a short period of time if he's only using the photos as a reference...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> The art director most likely got handled a budget and a schedule too. I think Onyx Path fans are a big spoiled because Rich Thomas got started in the RPG sphere as an artist and was the original WW's art director for a long time.<br /> <br /> Having looked at some of the artist's work that's not involved in all this, and before he scrubbed a bunch of stuff on Instagram:<br /> <br /> 1) He's actually really good. You can tell in the H5 core book art where it looks like he had more time. When he's no rushed his traces are far less obvious because they're far more mixed, and the finally results have quality and transformation so that even if you spot a trace, you don't really feel like it's as out of place as the W5 stuff has been.<br /> <br /> 2) He used to be really good about crediting his trace sources (that's what he scrubbed, as all his WoD work has not credit any trace sources like it should have).<br /> <br /> I'd imagine he was hired for all of this precisely because he can bang out decent quality tracer art fast. He still got overloaded and cut too many corners. The art director still didn't do proper oversight; esp. if the whole point was to higher someone that specializes in tracer art to go fast. Paradox's minimal official statements on it included saying their contracts have specific rules for tracer art. Which means they use tracer artists knowingly and have rules for proper licensing and crediting that weren't followed in this case.<br /> <br /> Like, most people loved this guy's work in H5, and even people going back and finding his tracers style at work, it's way less egregious. It really takes people going in and looking at it in far finer detail than how quickly people are finding sources for the W5 stuff. So I think we have to assume the plan was to use him for speed to get all this work done on schedule set higher up the food chain; even if it was still too big a lift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514441#post1514441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My boy is a Child of Gaia, Metis, Ahroun, so I'm sure you can imagine that W5 hasn't won a friend in me thus far. I can't wait to see the Children of Gaia preview!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Crinos-born have been stated to be out of the game for a long time now. So you were never converting that PC over despite any of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514445#post1514445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BTW does anyone have a link to this preview being posted on twitter? Or a link to people finding the trace origins?</div> </div> </div> </div>The earlier previews were being posted on Renegade's preorder page for W5, and on the WoD official Twitter account. The most recent preview is from a Renegade streaming preview, so there's no direct link for that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheCyberRecord/status/1662191013358899201\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://abs.twimg.com/x-web/assets/og/default-og.a2e144f0cf66.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheCyberRecord/status/1662191013358899201\" target=\"_blank\"> Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twitter.com/TheCyberRecord/status/1662191013358899201\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twitter.com/TheCyberRecord/status/1662191013358899201 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> This post is from a protected account. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That Twitter account has a lot of the original pieces... though I think people have stopped trying as the number of them has piled so high that everyone's just assuming they're all tracers at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514455#post1514455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It probably works like Hunger. So when you shift to Crinos you get two rage checks. You don't spend points, you get more points of rage making you less controllable and nastier to people around you until you hang out with someone to vent it. Also just now did I realise this kinda sounds like you take it out on the touchstones, but they probably meant it more about them being soothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the implications of this working much more like Hunger than Desperation, but you get rid of it by interacting with your Touchstones is... not great?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T06:47:00-07:00","id":1514464,"title":"","content":"Spending Willpower on the Crinos-form also gets another wrinkle because the Tribe-Bans are all about limiting your character's Willpower-healing. Through that Bans become an even bigger punishment. And considering how broad some Bans are (having to deal with every injustice as a Black Fury or always having to satisfy your curiosity as Ghost Council) dealing with Bans doesn't seem very fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514458#post1514458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art director most likely got handled a budget and a schedule too. I think Onyx Path fans are a big spoiled because Rich Thomas got started in the RPG sphere as an artist and was the original WW's art director for a long time.<br /> <br /> Having looked at some of the artist's work that's not involved in all this, and before he scrubbed a bunch of stuff on Instagram:<br /> <br /> 1) He's actually really good. You can tell in the H5 core book art where it looks like he had more time. When he's no rushed his traces are far less obvious because they're far more mixed, and the finally results have quality and transformation so that even if you spot a trace, you don't really feel like it's as out of place as the W5 stuff has been.<br /> <br /> 2) He used to be really good about crediting his trace sources (that's what he scrubbed, as all his WoD work has not credit any trace sources like it should have).<br /> <br /> I'd imagine he was hired for all of this precisely because he can bang out decent quality tracer art fast. He still got overloaded and cut too many corners. The art director still didn't do proper oversight; esp. if the whole point was to higher someone that specializes in tracer art to go fast. Paradox's minimal official statements on it included saying their contracts have specific rules for tracer art. Which means they use tracer artists knowingly and have rules for proper licensing and crediting that weren't followed in this case.<br /> <br /> Like, most people loved this guy's work in H5, and even people going back and finding his tracers style at work, it's way less egregious. It really takes people going in and looking at it in far finer detail than how quickly people are finding sources for the W5 stuff. So I think we have to assume the plan was to use him for speed to get all this work done on schedule set higher up the food chain; even if it was still too big a lift.</div> </div> </div> </div>And who knows how late last year they were even finished with the writing so that they could tell the artist which archetypes he was supposed to depict for the Tribe-sections, for example.<br /> <br /> They really have to hope that there's nothing else in the book on the same level as Tame Iti's face.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T10:24:25-07:00","id":1514477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514441#post1514441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's so juvenile, it's so instantly memeable, it's so... well it's just cringey.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me the so bad and cringy Devil May Cry reboot. Look at this (<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yP-UqnXSGDk\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yP-UqnXSGDk</a>\u200b), it's the same W5 writing quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T13:36:04-07:00","id":1514502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514374#post1514374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fuck...its a 'Rage Check' to transform....so based on our 12 month run with V5 there are going to be 2-3 Veil breaches per night and most of our times gonna be spent cleaning up murder scenes and erasing memories instead of just turning into a giant fucking wolf, (oh...wait hispo are just big dog size now aren't they?...which makes them larger or smaller than lupus depending on the subspecies of wolf? ) and tracking the mockery....</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess, and feel free to disagree, this would be a way to balance the use of the crinos which is quite strong, that way the crinos would be seen and used as a weapon of last resort, choosing to use Glabro or Hispo in the fight, I I'm not particularly against you making the character more difficult to control or limiting the crinos, but that seemed exaggerated to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:00:25-07:00","id":1514506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514502#post1514502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My guess, and feel free to disagree, this would be a way to balance the use of the crinos which is quite strong, that way the crinos would be seen and used as a weapon of last resort, choosing to use Glabro or Hispo in the fight, I I'm not particularly against you making the character more difficult to control or limiting the crinos, but that seemed exaggerated to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that this is a splatter game where you risk your life for something greater than yourself, not an incredibly inward-facing personal horror game. Vampires should eschew combat; why should werewolves, though? Is there a convincing argument for that when you're not a blood-swilling undead monster made of drugs that will stop at nothing for that next sweet, sweet hit of reanimation on your next night, never ending as long as you stay out of trouble and keep your head down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T14:03:07-07:00","id":1514507,"title":"","content":"In pre-W5 WtA, hispo is actually better for combat than crinos before you apply powers/etc. The higher Dex is better than the higher Str, and they get a damage bonus to bite attacks anyway to make up for the lower Str... while bites are -1 diff to hit.<br /> <br /> Crinos has a bigger advantage in flexibility because you get hands (or more importantly thumbs). Crinos can use Fetish weapons or guns meant to be mounted on military vehicles. There are way more Gifts that boost claw attacks than bite attacks. Crinos has better communication abilities (at least with other Garou). Basically, crinos embodied the concept of &quot;war form&quot; while hispo embodied the concept of &quot;killing form,&quot; in the old books. Crinos was the favored form because warfare is about more than pouncing on opponents and ripping their throat out, and the Garou were at war, not just killing things.<br /> <br /> Yes, that did leave glabro out in the cold, but that was more because it was originally meant to be more of the classic &quot;Wolf Man&quot; of Lon Chaney Jr. that's obviously not-human. Editions vary a bit here, but never really made sufficient use of glabro as a functional combat form for when normal folks were around to give it a more specific niche. The love/hate relationship the fandom has for the Fair Glabro Merit probably says a lot here: people love it because it make glabro really useful, but hate it because everyone wants it making it feel more obligatory than a fun unique quirk.<br /> <br /> W5 is very clearly moving to WtF's concept of what each form is supposed to be for, and this is fairly evidence in the form bonuses/penalties. However, Forsaken also changed the themes werewolves deal with, and how the forms work in WtF (esp. 2e) are made to reinforce those different themes. Themes we haven't seen expressed as W5's themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T17:02:39-07:00","id":1514525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514506#post1514506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that this is a splatter game where you risk your life for something greater than yourself, not an incredibly inward-facing personal horror game. Vampires should eschew combat; why should werewolves, though? Is there a convincing argument for that when you're not a blood-swilling undead monster made of drugs that will stop at nothing for that next sweet, sweet hit of reanimation on your next night, never ending as long as you stay out of trouble and keep your head down?</div> </div> </div> </div>I partially agree, it's weird for you to avoid using your Crinos form considering you'd be a werewolf, I particularly think it's more pratical for you to be worn out after each use than for you to literally go mad with rage every time you transform, but my point on you having a limitation for Crinos is the question of balancing with other creatures, because even a character that is not focused on combat would have at least two in strength and dexterity, with crinos this jumps to six and five which makes it have a great advantage against most creatures, the ST can manage with that, but that ruins the chances of crossplay for example, I imagine it was thinking about this detail that they created these limitations or they are thinking of expanding to other media and doing it that way would be more convenient, another thing they can add in the final product is that the crinos shape would be forbidden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T18:53:29-07:00","id":1514535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514525#post1514525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I partially agree, it's weird for you to avoid using your Crinos form considering you'd be a werewolf, I particularly think it's more pratical for you to be worn out after each use than for you to literally go mad with rage every time you transform, but my point on you having a limitation for Crinos is the question of balancing with other creatures, because even a character that is not focused on combat would have at least two in strength and dexterity, with crinos this jumps to six and five which makes it have a great advantage against most creatures, the ST can manage with that, but that ruins the chances of crossplay for example, I imagine it was thinking about this detail that they created these limitations or they are thinking of expanding to other media and doing it that way would be more convenient, another thing they can add in the final product is that the crinos shape would be forbidden.</div> </div> </div> </div>At this point, the only crossover play is with Vampire, and the end result of its demands are already terrible for the game on its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T19:05:54-07:00","id":1514536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514535#post1514535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point, the only crossover play is with Vampire, and the end result of its demands are already terrible for the game on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, I didn't see the sales, but the V5 looks more like a divider than a failure per se, I don't know how it is out there, but I've already met people who defend the V5 tooth and nail and say that it corrected all the errors in the editions previous ones, and only those who complain are the children who can't get four more levels because they have points left, I don't agree with them, but if there are actually people who prefer the V5 that already makes this argument questionable, having said that there may still be a way to crossover and nothing prevented them from already working on other versions of the other franchises, but that will also depend on the reception of W5 and nothing prevents other people from preferring this one to other versions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T19:15:00-07:00","id":1514538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514536#post1514536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, I didn't see the sales, but the V5 looks more like a divider than a failure per se, I don't know how it is out there, but I've already met people who defend the V5 tooth and nail and say that it corrected all the errors in the editions previous ones, and only those who complain are the children who can't get four more levels because they have points left, I don't agree with them, but if there are actually people who prefer the V5 that already makes this argument questionable, having said that there may still be a way to crossover and nothing prevented them from already working on other versions of the other franchises, but that will also depend on the reception of W5 and nothing prevents other people from preferring this one to other versions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a failure for Werewolf to be rewritten to be more like Vampire. I doubt that kind of half-measure is going to please anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T19:30:15-07:00","id":1514540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514538#post1514538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a failure for Werewolf to be rewritten to be more like Vampire. I doubt that kind of half-measure is going to please anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are a lot of things that don't seem attractive to me and even so it is successful in general and even if this less complicated proposal seems absurd, quite a lot to tell the truth, it can attract a lot of people, my reservation is with Crinos itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T01:30:48-07:00","id":1514557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514525#post1514525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I partially agree, it's weird for you to avoid using your Crinos form considering you'd be a werewolf, I particularly think it's more pratical for you to be worn out after each use than for you to literally go mad with rage every time you transform, but my point on you having a limitation for Crinos is the question of balancing with other creatures, because even a character that is not focused on combat would have at least two in strength and dexterity, with crinos this jumps to six and five which makes it have a great advantage against most creatures, the ST can manage with that, but that ruins the chances of crossplay for example, I imagine it was thinking about this detail that they created these limitations or they are thinking of expanding to other media and doing it that way would be more convenient, another thing they can add in the final product is that the crinos shape would be forbidden.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the themes/setting of WtA also should lead to a different perspective on what the forms do. WtF 2E solves that really well by re-orienting the forms around &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; as a paradigm. With WtA the forms are more complicated. For example, a human-born Garou has a different relationship with the Homid-form than a wolf-born Garou does. And then thematically what the forms also should reflect is that the Garou are warriors fighting for a cause. So, adding to the themes of the game it isn't strength where the Garou-Nation comes up short in their war against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> As for cross-play... H5 threw that out the window, I would say. The reason cross-play is easier with CofD-games is that it's set up with certain throughlines in all the games so that you have a common foundation for how things work. Just take Chronicle Tenets: In V5 they matter in how your character's Humanity is handled. Neither H5 nor W5 have integrated Chronicle Tenets into the mechanics of the game. Desperation and Danger in H5 are group-mechanics as well. With H5 I'm sure but with W5 I guess we'll have to wait and see but I assume that both games aren't set up with the idea of cross-play. When you play H5, you play H5 and when you play W5, you play W5. At most other splats will make an appearance as NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T01:53:20-07:00","id":1514559,"title":"","content":"And as hunter has demonstrated - they will not use the same mechanics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T08:55:43-07:00","id":1514579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514557#post1514557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the themes/setting of WtA also should lead to a different perspective on what the forms do. WtF 2E solves that really well by re-orienting the forms around &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; as a paradigm. With WtA the forms are more complicated. For example, a human-born Garou has a different relationship with the Homid-form than a wolf-born Garou does. And then thematically what the forms also should reflect is that the Garou are warriors fighting for a cause. So, adding to the themes of the game it isn't strength where the Garou-Nation comes up short in their war against the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> As for cross-play... H5 threw that out the window, I would say. The reason cross-play is easier with CofD-games is that it's set up with certain throughlines in all the games so that you have a common foundation for how things work. Just take Chronicle Tenets: In V5 they matter in how your character's Humanity is handled. Neither H5 nor W5 have integrated Chronicle Tenets into the mechanics of the game. Desperation and Danger in H5 are group-mechanics as well. With H5 I'm sure but with W5 I guess we'll have to wait and see but I assume that both games aren't set up with the idea of cross-play. When you play H5, you play H5 and when you play W5, you play W5. At most other splats will make an appearance as NPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't play H5 so I'll owe you that one, as for the first part, would you mind rephrasing? I've read this text about 10 times and I really can't understand the point you're making. What I can say is that since they want to simplify everything, so they put forms as being just forms, they are a resource with a cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T10:12:47-07:00","id":1514582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514579#post1514579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't play H5 so I'll owe you that one, as for the first part, would you mind rephrasing? I've read this text about 10 times and I really can't understand the point you're making. What I can say is that since they want to simplify everything, so they put forms as being just forms, they are a resource with a cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. So let me rephrase...<br /> <br /> In a mechanical sense, the forms are a bunch of bonuses and drawbacks. And so you want to create a balance between the number of bonuses and drawbacks but also not have bonuses that break every encounter with a foe in favor of the player or drawbacks that make something so unfun and/or punishing as to essentially be a motivation to avoid a particular mechanic/form. Creating balance in that sense is relevant.<br /> <br /> (Although, as an aside... I think one thing about W5 that will be interesting to see as well is the separation between &quot;simplified rules&quot; and &quot;expanded rules&quot;. For that reason, they released this pdf called &quot;Expanded Mechanics&quot; a year ago. The goal was to take these &quot;expanded mechanics&quot; out of the corebooks and put them into this splat-neutral &quot;Expanded Mechanics&quot; pdf. And one part of this divide is combat. Like, take this rule for the Crinos-form and spending Willpower per turn, for example. The simplified version of combat is never longer than three turns. The expanded version goes for a more tactical approach of different kinds of actions you can take and the combat lasts turn after turn after turn... until things get resolved. Will the W5 corebook address this divide? I guess, we\u2019ll see.)<br /> <br /> But the other side to these mechanical considerations of balance is the setting. And these oWOD-games have a lot going on in that department. Even with all the changes and &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;, you still have five Auspices, five Forms, two Breeds (human-born and wolf-born) and eleven Tribes. And the question is, from a story-perspective, why are there five Forms? How do five Forms fit into this setting? As mentioned, WtF 2E had &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; and so each form is a stage of the hunt which then in turn informs how you mechanically depict the forms. But the Garou of WtA are not the Uratha of WtF. The focus of WtA isn't on &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; but on the war against the Wyrm. And a Garou struggling with Rage isn't the same as a vampire trying to hold onto Humanity while struggling with their Hunger/Beast. The reason Garou are losing the war is that it isn't enough to just shift into Crinos and say &quot;Fuck you, Wyrm!&quot; (to quote the Ahroun-preview). So, making the Crinos-form an accessible physical-prowess-powerhouse shouldn\u2019t be that big of a deal. The physical/martial prowess of Garou isn't the thematic focus of the game. With WtF all the hunting-prowess of Uratha is balanced with a great rogues-gallery of antagonists that challenge that. With WtA the challenge is that the project is about saving the world and things aren't looking so good. And how do you change that within this setting? Physical prowess alone certainly isn\u2019t the solution. And part of the old setting were tragedies where said prowess was directed at the wrong targets even.<br /> <br /> With W5 it feels like the game is stepping away from being part of this epic world-saving project that's in crisis. You have things like &quot;The Garou-Nation has fallen&quot; and &quot;mid-Apocalypse&quot; but the mechanics also center the individual instead of worrying about the world. A lot of Rage-checks are mentioned on that char-sheet, then there are the WP-points for the Crinos-form and the Harano/Hauglosk-trackers are suggesting each Garou is in a constant struggle to either give up in despair or lose himself to Rage.<br /> <br /> And that brings us back to the Forms. I think the risk/benefit-analysis these Forms want to evoke is between the physical prowess of these forms - and the individual Garou's struggle with Rage. Not only in how it can make you lose control but in how it could advance your Harano- or Hauglosk-tracker. And that's very different from being a warrior for Gaia worrying about what needs to be done/how things in the Garou Nation have to change in order to save the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T11:25:12-07:00","id":1514587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514582#post1514582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure. So let me rephrase...<br /> <br /> In a mechanical sense, the forms are a bunch of bonuses and drawbacks. And so you want to create a balance between the number of bonuses and drawbacks but also not have bonuses that break every encounter with a foe in favor of the player or drawbacks that make something so unfun and/or punishing as to essentially be a motivation to avoid a particular mechanic/form. Creating balance in that sense is relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514582#post1514582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the other side to these mechanical considerations of balance is the setting. And these oWOD-games have a lot going on in that department. Even with all the changes and &quot;re-imagination, not continuation&quot;, you still have five Auspices, five Forms, two Breeds (human-born and wolf-born) and eleven Tribes. And the question is, from a story-perspective, why are there five Forms? How do five Forms fit into this setting? As mentioned, WtF 2E had &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; and so each form is a stage of the hunt which then in turn informs how you mechanically depict the forms. But the Garou of WtA are not the Uratha of WtF. The focus of WtA isn't on &quot;The wolf must hunt&quot; but on the war against the Wyrm. And a Garou struggling with Rage isn't the same as a vampire trying to hold onto Humanity while struggling with their Hunger/Beast. The reason Garou are losing the war is that it isn't enough to just shift into Crinos and say &quot;Fuck you, Wyrm!&quot; (to quote the Ahroun-preview). So, making the Crinos-form an accessible physical-prowess-powerhouse shouldn\u2019t be that big of a deal. The physical/martial prowess of Garou isn't the thematic focus of the game. With WtF all the hunting-prowess of Uratha is balanced with a great rogues-gallery of antagonists that challenge that. With WtA the challenge is that the project is about saving the world and things aren't looking so good. And how do you change that within this setting? Physical prowess alone certainly isn\u2019t the solution. And part of the old setting were tragedies where said prowess was directed at the wrong targets even.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this has already been well established, otherwise tribes like the SL and the GW would be irrelevant and just quirks from the players' point of view. Also I can only see the forms as resources and each form has it's uses, but for battle Crinos is better than the others and still can resolve pretty much anything. Glabro is only useful in tight spots or when you want to maintain cover and Hispo, I think is only better for chasing and ambushing. About power wrongdoings I guess this is something they want avoid here or unleast justify.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514582#post1514582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With W5 it feels like the game is stepping away from being part of this epic world-saving project that's in crisis. You have things like &quot;The Garou-Nation has fallen&quot; and &quot;mid-Apocalypse&quot; but the mechanics also center the individual instead of worrying about the world. A lot of Rage-checks are mentioned on that char-sheet, then there are the WP-points for the Crinos-form and the Harano/Hauglosk-trackers are suggesting each Garou is in a constant struggle to either give up in despair or lose himself to Rage.<br /> <br /> And that brings us back to the Forms. I think the risk/benefit-analysis these Forms want to evoke is between the physical prowess of these forms - and the individual Garou's struggle with Rage. Not only in how it can make you lose control but in how it could advance your Harano- or Hauglosk-tracker. And that's very different from being a warrior for Gaia worrying about what needs to be done/how things in the Garou Nation have to change in order to save the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much explain all I've heard it mentioned that paradox wanted WtA to be more personal, but that was difficult with the old theme so they brought in the apocalypse so the story stops being about the Garou nation and becomes about them, the Garou trying to survive, this also explains the limitation of Crinos, because without resorting to its strongest form and using it only when necessary makes survival a greater challenge and them avoiding getting lost in the rage is another challenge, and as you already explained, at this point the The Garou nation has fallen, the fight is over, Gaia has lost, and yes, I don't like Gaia very much.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T11:49:46-07:00","id":1514593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514587#post1514587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This pretty much explain all I've heard it mentioned that paradox wanted WtA to be more personal, but that was difficult with the old theme so they brought in the apocalypse so the story stops being about the Garou nation and becomes about them, the Garou trying to survive, this also explains the limitation of Crinos, because without resorting to its strongest form and using it only when necessary makes survival a greater challenge and them avoiding getting lost in the rage is another challenge, and as you already explained, at this point the The Garou nation has fallen, the fight is over, Gaia has lost, and yes, I don't like Gaia very much.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this &quot;personal&quot;. It's bandied around a lot, but Werewolf was always personal - it was a game about family and about protecting your own while fighting a war you didn't chose to be a part of. it was a game where you had to balance your relationships in a complex and volatile environment and where you had to make sure your loved ones would not get hurt by the fact that you're a monster withn. It was a game about protecting the last places where the world was still right and keeping them safe from interlopers that cannot be just killed off. The game was always personal, but set against a backdrop of a epic war in the service of something greater than yourself.<br /> <br /> W5 is about the service not meaning anything and the only element of the game that's relevant being the plots that we already had, just toned down with less mythic and spiritual components.<br /> <br /> And Apocalypse is not a joke. It's not a slow detoriation into nothingness. It's the spiritual and physical death of the world in which things from beyond destroy you from within and ensure that you do the worst things within your nature to others. The death of Gaia is the death of us all. So what is this Werewolf: The Apocalypse W5 claims to be?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T12:29:43-07:00","id":1514599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514593#post1514593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is this &quot;personal&quot;. It's bandied around a lot, but Werewolf was always personal - it was a game about family and about protecting your own while fighting a war you didn't chose to be a part of. it was a game where you had to balance your relationships in a complex and volatile environment and where you had to make sure your loved ones would not get hurt by the fact that you're a monster withn. It was a game about protecting the last places where the world was still right and keeping them safe from interlopers that cannot be just killed off. The game was always personal, but set against a backdrop of a epic war in the service of something greater than yourself.</div> </div> </div> </div>For anyone who thinks this gets in the way, I can only speak from experiences I've had, but I've only heard of one Garou character who cared about or mentioned family relationships and was an NPC in a Changeling game, otherwise it was Gaia first, then the rest the worst that many times the cause even seemed empty, just because yes. If you want my opinion I believe that Gaia is no different from the rest of the triad, if things were different then, would it be that if Gaia could she would not dominate everything and do the same as the Wyrm does if she had the chance? I think it's a scenario to think about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514593#post1514593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W5 is about the service not meaning anything and the only element of the game that's relevant being the plots that we already had, just toned down with less mythic and spiritual components.<br /> <br /> And Apocalypse is not a joke. It's not a slow detoriation into nothingness. It's the spiritual and physical death of the world in which things from beyond destroy you from within and ensure that you do the worst things within your nature to others. The death of Gaia is the death of us all. So what is this Werewolf: The Apocalypse W5 claims to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a guess, but I think he doesn't want to be anything but survival because when it's all over many times all you can do is move on, not necessarily for hope but for something simpler, nobody wants to die, or maybe since the world has ended and the mission no longer exists you should just do what you want, mad dog logic as they call it, either following your will or dying on your terms.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T14:11:09-07:00","id":1514614,"title":"","content":"I have not followed the developments, can someone explain the following to me:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I dont see a <b>Gnosis </b>trait on the sheet, is it gone now?</li> <li>I see a couple of RC values and the form changes mention a Rage Check, I assume it is the same. How does a <b>Rage Check</b> cost work now?</li> <li>On this Galliard I dont see a preset Rage value, does the auspice no longer grant a <b>Rage </b>stat?</li> <li>Is <b>Rage </b>at a maximum of 5 now?</li> <li>What does the <b>Harano track</b> measure?</li> <li>What does the<b> Hanglosk track </b>measure?</li> <li>There is no <b>Breed </b>value, is that no longer a thing?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 06-11-2023, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T15:33:06-07:00","id":1514625,"title":"","content":"1) While not fully confirmed previously, it was indicated that Gnosis was on the chopping block. It might still exist as a concept in the game, but it is at least no longer a trait.<br /> 2-6) We don't have full information on any of this. We can speculate based on V5 and H5, but that's about it. Rage does not seem to be something with a permanent rating, but we don't know if Auspice will impact Rage Checks, or if Auspice will be completely divorced from Rage in W5.<br /> 7) Mechanically, everyone is a homid in W5. You can choose to play a lupus if you want, but that's solely a character quirk with no impact on the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T16:08:08-07:00","id":1514630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514614#post1514614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not followed the developments, can someone explain the following to me:<br /> I see a couple of RC values and the form changes mention a Rage Check, I assume it is the same. How does a <b>Rage Check</b> cost work now?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, the funny thing about that is that &quot;Checks&quot; as a mechanic have come up precisely zero times in H5, so it's kinda weird to see Rage-Checks being plastered all over that char-sheet.<br /> <br /> But as for what Checks are, we go back to V5:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Checks: Unlike rolls, checks normally use a single die. The player makes a check by rolling one die, attempting to achieve a target number of 6 or higher.<br /> Vampire primarily uses checks to determine Hunger gain (see Hunger, feeding, and Rouse Checks, p. 211).<br /> Characters may not use Willpower to re-roll checks. Automatic wins and taking half never apply to checks.\u200b </div> </div> </div>So any time you see a Rage-Check mentioned, it means that you roll a die and there's a fifty/fifty chance Rage gets an extra dot... or loses one maybe... It's complicated...<br /> <br /> This is the tricky part: In Vampire, the equation's quite easy - Hunger 5 bad, Hunger 0 good (which meant that the fifty/fifty-outcomes were either Hunger rises by 1 or nothing happens). With Rage, you have Rage 0=bad (because then you're &quot;losing the wolf&quot;) and Rage 5=bad (because you're <i>too </i>angry). When the book comes out, we'll see how they handle that.<br /> <br /> Also, in V5 higher Blood Potency influenced Checks by letting you roll multiple dice and pick the highest for Checks. But what would be the equivalent for that in W5...?<br /> <br /> Once the book comes out, we can judge how well this idea of Rage as Hunger works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514614#post1514614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is <b>Rage </b>at a maximum of 5 now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514614#post1514614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does the <b>Harano track</b> measure? What does the<b> Hanglosk track </b>measure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Harano is extreme despair and Hauglosk is extreme urgency. But we don't know yet how exactly they interact with Rage or the game in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T16:15:00-07:00","id":1514631,"title":"","content":"Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T16:22:37-07:00","id":1514632,"title":"","content":"I already addressed this I think in another post, but I'll ask again. Is there any chance of someone making a fan-made W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T16:35:28-07:00","id":1514634,"title":"","content":"There's always a chance in theory? The big problem is all the people that don't like what we're seeing out of W5 are not inherently unified in what we'd want out of W5. There's a big difference between doing a bunch of homebrew to make the W5 that you would have wanted for yourself and your friends that you post publicly in case other people like it, publishing something in the STV that starts with either W20 or W5 as a base but changes a bunch of things you didn't like to create your ideal reset of the systems/setting, and publishing Werewolf: Legally Distinct from WW's IP that just dumps the official stuff completely to attract fans with the freedom of really starting fresh. The reality of what might happen depends a lot on the energy people have to commit to specific motivations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T00:27:18-07:00","id":1514658,"title":"","content":"I get a feeling that W5 will suffer the Changeling the Dreaming 2nd edition issue where people have to house rule a lot of things to have a cohesive setting.<br /> <br /> Because W5 so far has waffled between what it wants to be. All the character stuff is everyday life and very chill, but all the setting stuff is apocalypse and the nation falling.<br /> <br /> And here's the thing; You can be either or, not both. If you want a during the Apocalypse setting, that should look completely different from the 'balance your best and humanity' setting. The Nation falling should not look like the younger garou are GLAD it is gone.<br /> <br /> Then we add all the stuff from Forsaken, which is a setting with no time-limit or really anything bigger than local stuff.<br /> <br /> To me, the wanted game is clearly a game about balancing humanity and ferality with no external pressures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T01:34:35-07:00","id":1514664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514632#post1514632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already addressed this I think in another post, but I'll ask again. Is there any chance of someone making a fan-made W5?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagine someone might make a more faithful rework on vault. The tricky part is w20 already has everything you need. V5 kind of got away with a lot of changes because it was seen as return to what vtm was 'supposed' to be and some people like the hunger dice so it becomes easier to downplay the contreversial or outright bad decisions. Werewolf is going to struggle with that since the setting or plat didn't really deviate that much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T01:46:50-07:00","id":1514667,"title":"","content":"While we don't know how extensive it is yet, that one of the writers on a previous version of W5 that got canned has said he saw his work being used in the previews, we can only assume that part of the waffling is also because the final version of W5 is copying stuff from the earlier version without a lot of work put into normalizing the tone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T02:16:23-07:00","id":1514672,"title":"","content":"Additionally, due to the rushed development, W5 might be dealing with similar issues like H5. With H5 you had moments of oversights in rules-questions like when it proposed that you should use Desperation-Dice to bolster your Edge-rolls but never addressed how that interacted with the Creed-Fields. Or the entirety of the Danger-Track which is essentially a blank slate as a mechanic with the book just giving you examples of how an ST might use it. So one of the first things an ST for an H5 game has to do is decide how the Danger-Track actually works. And even with that, the book offers three <i>different </i>examples of how to apply the Danger-Track-rating to calculate the Difficulty of a roll. Meanwhile, the section in the rules on Difficulty never mentioned the Danger-Track at all.<br /> <br /> So, it's entirely possible that once we get the full book, the systems in W5 could feel just as half-baked as the ones in H5.<br /> <br /> And a case in point for that: The Harano- and Hauglosk-Tracks. That's why even with the Touchstones-preview I wasn't sure it would be two tracks. Because even if we don't know how exactly it works, having two separate tracks probably means that mechanically you could get into a situation where a particular Garou is equally close to be suffering from Harano or Hauglosk at the same time. So, you have a Garou with four dots in both tracks who is one dice-roll away from either suffering from extreme despair or extreme urgency. Talk about a roleplaying challenge!<br /> <br /> Of course, this could be solved by connecting the tracks and say &quot;Whenever you raise one, automatically lower the other.&quot; but then this would logically lead to yet another problem: That of telling the player that they should do something Harano-inducing to lower the Hauglosk-track or do something Hauglosk-inducing to lower the Harano-track.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T11:06:22-07:00","id":1514722,"title":"","content":"This is really not a game meant to be a fun punk power fantasy of venting your anger and frustration at the destruction of the environment. This just doesn't seem fun or particularly compelling, it's more pre packaged angst than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T11:08:33-07:00","id":1514724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514722#post1514722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really not a game meant to be a fun punk power fantasy of venting your anger and frustration at the destruction of the environment. This just doesn't seem fun or particularly compelling, it's more pre packaged angst than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, WOD games are supposed to be about personal horror, so coming with angst would be a plus I guess. By the way, that was a joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T12:06:28-07:00","id":1514728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514599#post1514599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For anyone who thinks this gets in the way, I can only speak from experiences I've had, but I've only heard of one Garou character who cared about or mentioned family relationships and was an NPC in a Changeling game, otherwise it was Gaia first, then the rest the worst that many times the cause even seemed empty, just because yes. If you want my opinion I believe that Gaia is no different from the rest of the triad, if things were different then, would it be that if Gaia could she would not dominate everything and do the same as the Wyrm does if she had the chance? I think it's a scenario to think about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that we have only one planet to live on and we are all products of it and have destroyed it utterly no matter the nigh infinite bounty she has provided us, one would think that were she a spiteful and power hungry thing as the Triat are we would have long since been destroyed or enslaved by her. There is an alternate setting where Gaia grows insane and needs to be fought by the heroic paladins of the Wyrm in the Revised Storyteller's handbook, but it's clearly NOT what the intended reading of Gaia is or what the whole setting lies on.<br /> <br /> Over 25 years of Werewolf I've had at least one character per chronicle decide to write themselves temporarily or permanently out of the game just to take care of their families, protect septs, kin or spirits they cared for and couldn't follow the rest of the cast into whatever hijinks or death they proceeded into. They will gladly have their characters die or stay in places which are unconductive to the game to protect what they value.This is a common theme as presented because if anything, Werewolves deeply care about the world and their part in it. It is in their nature as presented in the books themselves. Being Garou means being a part of the world and feeling its pain and looking for any possible way to make it stop.<br /> <br /> This is what makes the whole war personal, because you're fighting for your own and for what you believe in. You not seeing this is either due to a small sample of games or people with a shallow read of the material. It is in no way support for the thesis that &quot;Werewolf was not about personal stories&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514599#post1514599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Just a guess, but I think he doesn't want to be anything but survival because when it's all over many times all you can do is move on, not necessarily for hope but for something simpler, nobody wants to die, or maybe since the world has ended and the mission no longer exists you should just do what you want, mad dog logic as they call it, either following your will or dying on your terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's why this is not Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Because if the Apocalypse had happened there would not be ordinary people and ordinary jobs nor would the Garou be able to interact with a world that's just like ours only darker. Take a look into the book Apocalypse and have a gander what that actually means to all the worlds. This is some weird game where the authors wanted a minimum of connection to the past lore so that they could use the IP elements while making a street level urban fantasy game about riding the waves between Rage and Depression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:11:30-07:00","id":1514744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514724#post1514724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, WOD games are supposed to be about personal horror, so coming with angst would be a plus I guess. By the way, that was a joke.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Vampire is supposed to be about personal horror. The other games had different taglines following &quot;A Storytelling Game of...&quot;.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: Savage Horror<br /> Mage: Reality On The Brink<br /> Wraith: Passion and Horror<br /> Changeling: Modern Fantasy<br /> <br /> There is, in fact, an essay about this in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook. The cliff's notes of this is that, while you can play around with those other themes, W:tA is fundamentally built around how anyone can die horribly at any time. The essay even explicitly notes that crossover characters in W:tA are basically fucking around until they find out. Typically, by being turned into an unrecognizable corpse. The horror of Werewolf is that there's a closed casket funeral waiting for you at the end of your run, and you have to fight like hell to keep that from happening sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> (The combat in the what-of-Undertale-was-Berserk dark adventure PC game Fear and Hunger comes to mind, where you're perennially aiming to cut off the swordarm or what have you of dangerous enemies before they cut off your limbs... and the end goal for both sides is to unbalance and behead your foe.)<br /> <br /> A W5 that actually realized that wouldn't be trying to strangle the game by being a street-level Vampire knockoff with palette-swapped protagonists, it would be trying to tackle Violence, front and center. A WoD5 that actually realized the multiple themes across the games, too, wouldn't be trying to flatten everything, but maybe provide a take on the different themes relative to the game itself, so that we can stop having quite the same record-scratching disconnect between, say, Mage and everything else with the former starts talking about, to give just one out-there example, orbital prisons holding the cast of Little Witch Academia captive by immortal alchemists who are still in charge of determining the trajectory of modern scientific advancement from their otherworldly redoubts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:39:21-07:00","id":1514749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514744#post1514744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, Vampire is supposed to be about personal horror. The other games had different taglines following &quot;A Storytelling Game of...&quot;.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: Savage Horror<br /> Mage: Reality On The Brink<br /> Wraith: Passion and Horror<br /> Changeling: Modern Fantasy<br /> <br /> There is, in fact, an essay about this in the Revised Storyteller's Handbook. The cliff's notes of this is that, while you can play around with those other themes, W:tA is fundamentally built around how anyone can die horribly at any time. The essay even explicitly notes that crossover characters in W:tA are basically fucking around until they find out. Typically, by being turned into an unrecognizable corpse. The horror of Werewolf is that there's a closed casket funeral waiting for you at the end of your run, and you have to fight like hell to keep that from happening sooner rather than later.<br /> <br /> (The combat in the what-of-Undertale-was-Berserk dark adventure PC game Fear and Hunger comes to mind, where you're perennially aiming to cut off the swordarm or what have you of dangerous enemies before they cut off your limbs... and the end goal for both sides is to unbalance and behead your foe.)<br /> <br /> A W5 that actually realized that wouldn't be trying to strangle the game by being a street-level Vampire knockoff with palette-swapped protagonists, it would be trying to tackle Violence, front and center. A WoD5 that actually realized the multiple themes across the games, too, wouldn't be trying to flatten everything, but maybe provide a take on the different themes relative to the game itself, so that we can stop having quite the same record-scratching disconnect between, say, Mage and everything else with the former starts talking about, to give just one out-there example, orbital prisons holding the cast of Little Witch Academia captive by immortal alchemists who are still in charge of determining the trajectory of modern scientific advancement from their otherworldly redoubts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never saw or played a game of WtA where the fear of death seems important, the only thing that resembles that was a PC that I made and was monster and no one liked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T13:49:51-07:00","id":1514751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514728#post1514728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's why this is not Werewolf: the Apocalypse. Because if the Apocalypse had happened there would not be ordinary people and ordinary jobs nor would the Garou be able to interact with a world that's just like ours only darker. Take a look into the book Apocalypse and have a gander what that actually means to all the worlds. This is some weird game where the authors wanted a minimum of connection to the past lore so that they could use the IP elements while making a street level urban fantasy game about riding the waves between Rage and Depression.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't have the book, but a saw something in the wikia, I know this isn't good as the book, but it's what I have, so, let's go with it. It's a odyssey and I ask to myself in what battlefield I will die, because I can no see hope in survive or in a purpose after that and strangely I think about end where someone asks for Gaia to don't be more a Garou, just a wolf. Strange, I kno, also changed the topic, sorry. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:02:59-07:00","id":1514755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514749#post1514749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never saw or played a game of WtA where the fear of death seems important, the only thing that resembles that was a PC that I made and was monster and no one liked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I've never played in a game of W:tA where the characters bemoaned their existences and adopted self-serving platitudes like &quot;a monster I am lest a monster I be&quot;. I have played in a game where a battle scar was had, though (that reactor in the Weird Science adventure of Valkenburg Foundation is a hell of a hit), and that's something that really should have been revisited with modern mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T14:26:54-07:00","id":1514759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514749#post1514749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Never saw or played a game of WtA where the fear of death seems important, the only thing that resembles that was a PC that I made and was monster and no one liked it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know. I'm curious. How much Werewolf did you play and/or Storytell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T15:09:57-07:00","id":1514765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514759#post1514759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know. I'm curious. How much Werewolf did you play and/or Storytell?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen several hours of games, but playing around here is complicated and I don't want to pay to join a group. Summary of the story I participated in two chronicles, a few sessions each, with different groups. I've never been a storyteller, I wanted to, but I don't think I'm good at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T15:19:17-07:00","id":1514767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514755#post1514755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I've never played in a game of W:tA where the characters bemoaned their existences and adopted self-serving platitudes like &quot;a monster I am lest a monster I be&quot;. I have played in a game where a battle scar was had, though (that reactor in the Weird Science adventure of Valkenburg Foundation is a hell of a hit), and that's something that really should have been revisited with modern mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't understand the reference","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T17:57:55-07:00","id":1514783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514767#post1514767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't understand the reference</div> </div> </div> </div>It turns out that a metric ton equivalent of TNT does a lot of damage (30 dice!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T23:32:13-07:00","id":1514802,"title":"","content":"Of course the fear of death is important i WtA. Why? Many reasons, catch few examples:<br /> <br /> 1. Ahroun - If I die who will protect my kin, my familly, our sacred places. I am the last bastion between things that are coming and my pack, my familly. My death is my failure.<br /> <br /> 2. Galiard - if I die would someone remember me before I became known? What would happen with my stories, with my knowledge, I did not shared everything with others, many heroes will die with me cause there will be no one who would remember them and stories about them. <br /> <br /> 3. Philodox - without me everything would be shred to pieces. The promises I made, the pacts I 've done, the peace I have achived in the sept was long and hard work and I know that without my guide all I have build will be lost cause I have not found young form my replacement. One side would not respect our Laws, the other will use Litany to achive their goals, without judge thee will be animosity.<br /> <br /> 4. Theurge - the spirits , my friends are at my service not because they are forced to do so, or cause of debt. They know I am their protector and friend, and so they are our sept eyes and ears. With my death they will abandon their role. Without me out pack will be blind in Umbra. And it dwells in the darkness , it will came, It fears me, but when I'll be gone it will unleash it's wrath.<br /> <br /> 5. Ragabash - who will question the ways when I'll be gone. Who'll take care of my pack, my sept, my familly. I am the glue that stick them together, I think that they will miss me and maby they will break apart or jump to their throats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-12T23:44:54-07:00","id":1514804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514765#post1514765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've seen several hours of games, but playing around here is complicated and I don't want to pay to join a group. Summary of the story I participated in two chronicles, a few sessions each, with different groups. I've never been a storyteller, I wanted to, but I don't think I'm good at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you have a sample size of two, from the sounds of it, not very long running games?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/8fsIR2T.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13566-kalzky","name":"Kalzky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13566_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T02:34:16-07:00","id":1514812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kalzky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514804#post1514804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you have a sample size of two, from the sounds of it, not very long running games?</div> </div> </div> </div>Started in 2015 or 2016 with VtM, stayed with a group until be expelled in 2019, and played WtA after, but don't played anything in last two to three years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T03:23:23-07:00","id":1514816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514802#post1514802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course the fear of death is important i WtA. Why? Many reasons, catch few examples:<br /> <br /> 1. Ahroun - If I die who will protect my kin, my familly, our sacred places. I am the last bastion between things that are coming and my pack, my familly. My death is my failure.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, if you should be more afraid of failing than of dying in this case, Gaia has given you a service and you must do it, death is just a consequence, at least that's how it seemed to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Galiard - if I die would someone remember me before I became known? What would happen with my stories, with my knowledge, I did not shared everything with others, many heroes will die with me cause there will be no one who would remember them and stories about them. </div> </div> </div>This one I won't even comment on because it would be very mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Philodox - without me everything would be shred to pieces. The promises I made, the pacts I 've done, the peace I have achived in the sept was long and hard work and I know that without my guide all I have build will be lost cause I have not found young form my replacement. One side would not respect our Laws, the other will use Litany to achive their goals, without judge thee will be animosity. </div> </div> </div>They already do, just behind your back. Seriously though, the philodox I saw were more smooth talkers than mediators.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. Theurge - the spirits , my friends are at my service not because they are forced to do so, or cause of debt. They know I am their protector and friend, and so they are our sept eyes and ears. With my death they will abandon their role. Without me out pack will be blind in Umbra. And it dwells in the darkness , it will came, It fears me, but when I'll be gone it will unleash it's wrath. </div> </div> </div>Same case as the Galliard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Ragabash - who will question the ways when I'll be gone. Who'll take care of my pack, my sept, my familly. I am the glue that stick them together, I think that they will miss me and maby they will break apart or jump to their throats. </div> </div> </div>A well-played Ragabash is what we call the devil's lawyer, if he is what unites it is because of the collective hatred that others have for him. Seriously, I've never seen anyone play a Ragabash like that and I don't blame anyone who does because I already know how toxic people can be.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T03:44:27-07:00","id":1514818,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> I'm sorry you had shitty experiences playing Werewolf. The views on how the Auspices work are essentially the worst stereotypes and played in an incredibly sad way and seem to have left you with a very skewed way of what Werewolf is. Because everything I see from you, I'd recommend looking into it deeper, look into Apocalypse and the Book of Auspices for starters. <br /> <br /> Also, if you're actually interested in Werewolf, you should consider running it once you get into the setting a bit more. Just because you don't have a lot of experience doesn't mean you are unable to run a game. And remember, you at least have a template of what not to do if you're keen on keeping your players happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T04:00:56-07:00","id":1514821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514818#post1514818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> I'm sorry you had shitty experiences playing Werewolf. The views on how the Auspices work are essentially the worst stereotypes and played in an incredibly sad way and seem to have left you with a very skewed way of what Werewolf is. Because everything I see from you, I'd recommend looking into it deeper, look into Apocalypse and the Book of Auspices for starters.<br /> <br /> Also, if you're actually interested in Werewolf, you should consider running it once you get into the setting a bit more. Just because you don't have a lot of experience doesn't mean you are unable to run a game. And remember, you at least have a template of what not to do if you're keen on keeping your players happy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. I've been running WtA for 30 years now and I can't really relate to any of Psicoses experiences with the game. I'm sorry they had such terrible experiences but it does mean I don't recognise the game they are describing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T04:39:27-07:00","id":1514822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514818#post1514818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> I'm sorry you had shitty experiences playing Werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thirded<br /> Like the my learned and esteemed colleagues I'm also an ancient Storyteller and like them, I mostly had good experiences with the game - had a fair share of problems, of course, but nothing serious.<br /> Sorry mate you had bad experiences<br /> But as as <b><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai\">Asmodai</a></b>\u200b said, don't give up! <br /> The lack of experience doesn't mean you can't be a Storyteller... hell, we ALL been in that shoe!<br /> Every Storyteller had to start somewhere and had nothing just a handfull of suplements and bunch of ideas (and a few potential victims... err.... players who were willing to be guinea pigs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> You just have the muster up the courage to start and you will be fine! <br /> And yeah, use your bad experience what avoid and always consult with ypur players!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T05:17:26-07:00","id":1514827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514816#post1514816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In my opinion, if you should be more afraid of failing than of dying in this case, Gaia has given you a service and you must do it, death is just a consequence, at least that's how it seemed to me.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah it might be. But Not every garou think this way. Bone Gnawer survival instinct may be stronger.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514816#post1514816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one I won't even comment on because it would be very mean.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It won't offend me, feel free to comment in any way. In my opinion and as I learned from the books galiard role is to see, remember and tell about what he saw, cause there's oral tradition to exchange stories rather than write them among garou. With death of pack's galiard it's possible that many things they achieved would be forgotten, and with it renown /glory of the pack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514816#post1514816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A well-played Ragabash is what we call the devil's lawyer, if he is what unites it is because of the collective hatred that others have for him. Seriously, I've never seen anyone play a Ragabash like that and I don't blame anyone who does because I already know how toxic people can be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've played with few ragabash players and everyone told me that's the hardest archetype to play and everyone was different from another. Example I wrote about was one of the players and he was Children of Gaia so ..<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T05:21:38-07:00","id":1514829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514827#post1514827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I've played with few ragabash players and everyone told me that's the hardest archetype to play and everyone was different from another. Example I wrote about was one of the players and he was Children of Gaia so ..<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have an informal with ragabash that if they're going to be a trickster type then they have to be funny irl. I can tolerate a lot at the table but I'll be buggered if I'm going to be a captive audience to your failed attempt at wit.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T05:33:06-07:00","id":1514831,"title":"","content":"I love the ragabash possibilities but I often don't like what players do with them and during my experience I've been playing with only one player who fit the role perfectly - pack centered and helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 06-13-2023, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T06:14:58-07:00","id":1514836,"title":"","content":"The way I describe the Auspice to players is to first think of a Ragabash's duty to question things. In other words, they are there to offer the one perspective nobody else seems to consider. Now how you present that perspective is what's up to the player. But they don't have to be the trickster or tell jokes or play pranks on others.<br /> <br /> And yeah, there's nothing worse than someone trying to play a &quot;funny&quot; character who doesn't have a strong sense of humor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T12:18:46-07:00","id":1514870,"title":"","content":"What's a strong sense of humor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T13:55:16-07:00","id":1514877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514870#post1514870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a strong sense of humor?</div> </div> </div> </div>When a bunch of Wyrm-Influenced Corporation majority shareholders walk into open manholes and die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T17:02:15-07:00","id":1514898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514877#post1514877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When a bunch of Wyrm-Influenced Corporation majority shareholders walk into open manholes and die.</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's a psychotic sense of humor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T18:58:12-07:00","id":1514906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514898#post1514898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's a psychotic sense of humor?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?client=firefox-b-1-d&amp;q=quote+mel+brooks+tragedy+is+when+I+cut+my+finger\" target=\"_blank\">Not really, no.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T22:55:53-07:00","id":1514919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514870#post1514870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's a strong sense of humor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Timing, knowing your audience, joke-structure...<br /> <br /> There are lots of things you can get wrong when you're trying to be funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T04:05:44-07:00","id":1514934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514919#post1514919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Timing, knowing your audience, joke-structure...<br /> <br /> There are lots of things you can get wrong when you're trying to be funny.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following your discussion on the rpg.net W5 thread.<br /> <br /> I may be misunderstanding the terms being used but are the two arguing against your viewpoint basically just saying that your supposed to just ignore the mechanics and make up stuff even if its not supported by the actual PC stats? <br /> <br /> Its just a weird mindset where not being able to attempt an action is stated to be the same thing as being able to attempt that action or stating that not having the stats needed to attempt something should just be ignored and the results determined via ST fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T04:30:46-07:00","id":1514938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514934#post1514934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Following your discussion on the rpg.net W5 thread.<br /> <br /> I may be misunderstanding the terms being used but are the two arguing against your viewpoint basically just saying that your supposed to just ignore the mechanics and make up stuff even if its not supported by the actual PC stats?<br /> <br /> Its just a weird mindset where not being able to attempt an action is stated to be the same thing as being able to attempt that action or stating that not having the stats needed to attempt something should just be ignored and the results determined via ST fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is about the Crinos-Form and its rule of &quot;Social and Stealth: Fail&quot;, just so everybody knows.<br /> <br /> From their viewpoint, you're not &quot;automatically failing&quot; the roll because what it's actually trying to do is say that in Crinos-Form you're incapable of using the skill/do an action associated with it. Someone can feel intimidated by you being a Crinos but you in Crinos Form can't intimidate them as a conscious action. With the idea that you're doing physical actions to overcome obstacles, not social ones.<br /> <br /> My two points are: 1) The language should be changed because what they're describing isn't &quot;automatically failing a roll&quot;. 2) There's already a steep enough price associated with shifting into Crinos plus the ticking clock of WP-damage until you automatically suffer from Frenzy. A penalty would be okay here as well but outright banning the use of social skills even before you suffer from Frenzy goes too far in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T04:34:53-07:00","id":1514940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514938#post1514938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is about the Crinos-Form and its rule of &quot;Social and Stealth: Fail&quot;, just so everybody knows.<br /> <br /> From their viewpoint, you're not &quot;automatically failing&quot; the roll because what it's actually trying to do is say that in Crinos-Form you're incapable of using the skill/do an action associated with it. Someone can feel intimidated by you being a Crinos but you in Crinos Form can't intimidate them as a conscious action. With the idea that you're doing physical actions to overcome obstacles, not social ones.<br /> <br /> My two points are: 1) The language should be changed because what they're describing isn't &quot;automatically failing a roll&quot;. 2) There's already a steep enough price associated with shifting into Crinos plus the ticking clock of WP-damage until you automatically suffer from Frenzy. A penalty would be okay here as well but outright banning the use of social skills even before you suffer from Frenzy goes too far in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fully agree with you on all that, there was also something about Mechanically Crinos are faster than lupus and Hispo but their statements indicated that wasn't an issue because the ST can just say they aren't regardless of the mechanics?<br /> <br /> Apologies for bringing it over here, though relevant I think, but I am unable to post there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T04:46:45-07:00","id":1514942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514940#post1514940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fully agree with you on all that, there was also something about Mechanically Crinos are faster than lupus and Hispo but their statements indicated that wasn't an issue because the ST can just say they aren't regardless of the mechanics?<br /> <br /> Apologies for bringing it over here, though relevant I think, but I am unable to post there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it gets a bit wacky if you're really rules-lawyering it. I mean, the Crinos gives a four-dice-bonus to all physical actions but auto-fails Stealth. But one of the physical skills is... Larceny. So technically a Crinos is really good at picking locks.<br /> <br /> Personally, whenever I come up with houserules something like this would make me go back and rethink the approach. When following the rule as written can get you into weird places like this then you're just creating extra work for whenever a player brings it up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-14T04:56:55-07:00","id":1514944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1514362-ahroun-auspice-filled-out-character-sheet-w5-preview?p=1514942#post1514942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, it gets a bit wacky if you're really rules-lawyering it. I mean, the Crinos gives a four-dice-bonus to all physical actions but auto-fails Stealth. But one of the physical skills is... Larceny. So technically a Crinos is really good at picking locks.<br /> <br /> Personally, whenever I come up with houserules something like this would make me go back and rethink the approach. When following the rule as written can get you into weird places like this then you're just creating extra work for whenever a player brings it up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense to me. Thanks for your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"